{"seq":45,"slug":"message-queues-event-driven","title":"消息队列与事件驱动架构","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven","rating":{"composite":3.84,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 消息队列与事件驱动架构\n\n当两个服务直接互相调用时，调用方的命运被被调用方绑死：对方变慢，你跟着变慢；对方宕机，你的请求当场失败。消息队列把这条同步链路切断，在中间塞入一段可以缓冲、可以削峰、可以重放的存储。本 hub 讲的就是这段「中间存储」如何工作，以及围绕它生长出来的整套事件驱动架构。\n\n四章是一条明确的递进线。第一章「基础」把地基打牢：为什么消息传递能解耦、队列与主题这两种存储模型有什么本质区别、以及任何分布式消息系统都绕不开的投递保证（至多一次、至少一次、恰好一次）。这一章建立的词汇会贯穿全书——后面所有关于重试、幂等、顺序的讨论，根都扎在这里。\n\n第二章「消息模式」从「能不能传」上升到「怎么传得聪明」。发布订阅与点对点决定了一条消息被一个还是多个消费者拿到；路由与过滤让 broker 替你做分流，而不是把所有消息广播给所有人再让消费者自己丢弃；死信与重试则回答了那个最现实的问题：消息处理失败了怎么办，既不能无限阻塞，也不能默默丢弃。\n\n第三章「事件驱动架构」把视角从单条消息拉高到整个系统。事件驱动架构（EDA）是一种以「已发生的事实」为中心来组织服务协作的风格；事件溯源把这种思想推到极致，让事件日志本身成为系统的唯一真相源；CQRS 则顺势把读和写拆成两条独立演化的路径。这三者常被一起提及，但它们解决的是不同层次的问题，本章会把边界讲清楚。\n\n第四章「系统与实践」落到地面。市面上的 Kafka、RabbitMQ、NATS、各家云托管队列各有取舍，选型要看吞吐、顺序、保留这几个维度；顺序与幂等是把第一章的理论变成可运行代码的关键工程手段；监控与运维则保证这套系统上线后你还能睡得着觉——消费滞后、死信堆积、端到端延迟都需要被看见。\n\n读法上，建议至少顺读第一章再跳读。投递保证、顺序、幂等这三个概念互相缠绕，分散在 1.3、4.2 两篇里详述，其余各篇遇到时只点到为止并交叉链接过去，避免重复。读完全 hub，你应当能独立判断一个业务场景该不该上消息队列、该选哪种模式、以及上线后该盯哪些指标。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"messaging-overview","title":"消息传递与解耦","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/foundations/messaging-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"queues-topics","title":"队列与主题模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/foundations/queues-topics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"delivery-guarantees","title":"投递保证","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/foundations/delivery-guarantees"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"patterns","title":"消息模式","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"pubsub-pointtopoint","title":"发布订阅与点对点","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/patterns/pubsub-pointtopoint"},{"seq":2,"slug":"routing-filtering","title":"路由与过滤","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/patterns/routing-filtering"},{"seq":3,"slug":"dead-letter-retry","title":"死信与重试","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/patterns/dead-letter-retry"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"event-driven","title":"事件驱动架构","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/event-driven","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"event-driven-architecture","title":"事件驱动架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/event-driven/event-driven-architecture"},{"seq":2,"slug":"event-sourcing","title":"事件溯源","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/event-driven/event-sourcing"},{"seq":3,"slug":"cqrs","title":"CQRS 模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/event-driven/cqrs"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"systems","title":"系统与实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/systems","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"brokers-comparison","title":"消息中间件对比","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/systems/brokers-comparison"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ordering-idempotency","title":"顺序与幂等","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/systems/ordering-idempotency"},{"seq":3,"slug":"observability-ops","title":"监控与运维","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/message-queues-event-driven/systems/observability-ops"}]}]}